      "claim": "Encainide, a piperidine anilide, had F=76-78% in cirrhosis (C03, C06, C12), with >2-fold higher than healthy extensive metabolizers (C21), supporting high F for this piperidine amide class.",
      "card_ids": ["C03", "C06", "C12", "C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 fentanyl oral exposure record C28 shows measurable systemic exposure after a 300 µg oral dose, consistent with oral absorption of the fentanyl class.",
      "card_ids": ["C28"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 fentanyl P-gp record C53/C59 shows fentanyl is a P-gp substrate, but with high Papp and modest efflux; this is a mechanistic caveat, not affirmative evidence for F<20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C53", "C59"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 high-permeability/no-efflux records for basic piperidines (C50, C51) support the absorption component.",
      "card_ids": ["C50", "C51"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "weakened",
      "card_ids": ["C53", "C59", "C56"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "Fentanyl P-gp record does not provide a control efflux ratio or F value; P-gp substrate status alone is not a direct F result.",
    "Closest opioid contexts were measured in cirrhosis; normal-condition F is inferred with uncertainty.",
    "No query-specific first-pass metabolism, solubility, or intestinal metabolism data.",
    "L5 records are for other molecules; transferability is limited."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high: meperidine and encainide contexts support F>20%, fentanyl oral exposure supports absorption, and L5 fentanyl P-gp substrate status is only a modest mechanistic caveat. No affirmative evidence supports F<20%; confidence moderate."
}

